I walk over to the bakery counter.
The smell is very good.
I like cakes.
And I really like cinnamon pastries.
A baker stands behind the counter.
The baker looks at me.
He smiles.
"What would you like to have?" the baker asks.
I point at a cinnamon pastry.
The pastry looks delicious.
"I would like to have a cinnamon pastry, please," I say.
"Yes, of course," the baker says.
He takes the pastry.
He puts the pastry in a bag.
He hands the bag over the counter.
"Here you go," he says.
I take the bag.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I put the bag down into the basket.
